{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Runs a saved FLOW command once and reports which cases of its nextcase chain ran. Returns {status, result, path, cases}: result is the envelope a plain run returns (same auth check, cast_params and format_result as app.app.exec); path is [{case, end, ms, msg?}], one entry per case executed, root first, where end is next (a next rule fired and the run moved on), done, terminate (a wired return terminal was never delivered), fail (a fail rule fired) or panic. It uses flowlang's own interpreter one case at a time: each case runs with a sentinel nextcase that only marks the jump, so every op executes exactly once in the normal order, with outputs accumulated across cases as Code::execute does. A next rule firing in the last case is reported as an I-4 error instead of panicking. Runs the SAVED body, not unsaved editor changes. Inputs: lib, ctl, cmd name the flow command; args are its arguments (JSONObject, coerced by the command's param types); nn_sessionid is filled in by the framework (pass \"\" from javascript).","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse std::panic;\nuse crate::app::service::init::format_result;\nuse crate::security::security::init::check_auth;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"args","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"msuuqu1a165e00598r1161","readers":[],"time":1792793397925,"username":"system","writers":[]}